{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegUPuYfcoT5G4m8XCGjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JxK6pXVfqgBb9pf8wDBZEX","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers.md","old_string":"**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].","new_string":"**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity.\n\n**MUTATION-DRIVE the inherited regression, don't just run it.** Running the new\ntest proves it passes, not that it bites — an `== 0` / `exit 0` assertion can be\nreading silence. Revert the exact mechanism under test (round 036: `rglob` ->\n`glob` in `gen_verdict_rollup._extra`), confirm the test FAILS *with the symptom\nthe finding named* (here `fresh (1 review scope(s))` while a stale nested output\nsat in the tree), then restore. Cheap, and it is the only step that separates a\nreal regression from one wired to the fixture. Also drive the shipped flow on\nthe real repo, not only `tmp_path`.\n\n**Trap when driving generators on a work branch:** `docs/reviews/rollup/` is\ntrunk-owned (`docs/stack.ini [generated]` = `verdictrollup`), so it is correctly\nABSENT and untracked on a lane — running the generator to verify it creates\nuntracked residue you must `rm -rf` afterward, and its `--check` will report\nevery rollup stale simply because none exists there yet. That is not drift.\nRelated: [[tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]],\n[[record-post-close-verification-in-log-d]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":81240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b2db2ef-e0c7-48d3-b559-2dce3466f1be","uuid":"6795ff9a-4fb9-4d95-b310-ef5a75d0f6c5","request_id":"req_011CegUPtZ8kNBPP3kVaYDWJ"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxK6pXVfqgBb9pf8wDBZEX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b2db2ef-e0c7-48d3-b559-2dce3466f1be","uuid":"012ee897-f126-447f-9486-f05841b917eb","timestamp":"2026-09-03T12:03:36.462Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers.md","oldString":"**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].","newString":"**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity.\n\n**MUTATION-DRIVE the inherited regression, don't just run it.** Running the new\ntest proves it passes, not that it bites — an `== 0` / `exit 0` assertion can be\nreading silence. Revert the exact mechanism under test (round 036: `rglob` ->\n`glob` in `gen_verdict_rollup._extra`), confirm the test FAILS *with the symptom\nthe finding named* (here `fresh (1 review scope(s))` while a stale nested output\nsat in the tree), then restore. Cheap, and it is the only step that separates a\nreal regression from one wired to the fixture. Also drive the shipped flow on\nthe real repo, not only `tmp_path`.\n\n**Trap when driving generators on a work branch:** `docs/reviews/rollup/` is\ntrunk-owned (`docs/stack.ini [generated]` = `verdictrollup`), so it is correctly\nABSENT and untracked on a lane — running the generator to verify it creates\nuntracked residue you must `rm -rf` afterward, and its `--check` will report\nevery rollup stale simply because none exists there yet. That is not drift.\nRelated: [[tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]],\n[[record-post-close-verification-in-log-d]].","originalFile":"---\nname: verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers\ndescription: \"Re-drive a rework finding's already-landed fix instead of reading it; tightening one of two paired readers silently wedges the other\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 0c77d95a-257c-47ee-9c6a-bf0d0ac81ad1\n---\n\nWhen a worker session inherits a REWORK FINDING that a prior commit on the same\nbranch already fixed, **re-drive the fix rather than confirm it by reading the\ndiff**. On WI-579 the round-022 MAJOR was closed at `c939d49c`; driving it on\nthe suite's own fixture surfaced a NEW major defect the fix itself introduced.\n\nThe specific trap, which recurred three times on one lane (rounds 007, 015,\n022→023): where two readers answer one question from two sides — the merge gate\n(`integrate._verdict_gate`) and the loop's owed-derivation\n(`agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence`) — **tightening one silently wedges the\nlane**, because the other still clears on the looser rule. The lane then\nschedules nothing while the gate refuses, or draws a round the gate won't read.\n\n**Why:** a passing suite proves neither reader wrong; the disagreement is only\nvisible when you drive BOTH at the same fixture state and compare answers.\n\n**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":6,"newStart":26,"newLines":23,"lines":[" and asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in"," the leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are"," legitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the","-divergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:","+divergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity.","+","+**MUTATION-DRIVE the inherited regression, don't just run it.** Running the new","+test proves it passes, not that it bites — an `== 0` / `exit 0` assertion can be","+reading silence. Revert the exact mechanism under test (round 036: `rglob` ->","+`glob` in `gen_verdict_rollup._extra`), confirm the test FAILS *with the symptom","+the finding named* (here `fresh (1 review scope(s))` while a stale nested output","+sat in the tree), then restore. Cheap, and it is the only step that separates a","+real regression from one wired to the fixture. Also drive the shipped flow on","+the real repo, not only `tmp_path`.","+","+**Trap when driving generators on a work branch:** `docs/reviews/rollup/` is","+trunk-owned (`docs/stack.ini [generated]` = `verdictrollup`), so it is correctly","+ABSENT and untracked on a lane — running the generator to verify it creates","+untracked residue you must `rm -rf` afterward, and its `--check` will report","+every rollup stale simply because none exists there yet. That is not drift.","+Related: [[tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan]],"," [[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],","-[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].","+[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]],","+[[record-post-close-verification-in-log-d]]."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegUQvhedVyNJqRQWZfnn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The round-036 rework was already committed by session 037. Rather than trust the diff, I verified it — and the verification is the substance of this session.\n\n## What I found\n\n**The fix is real and complete.** The finding asked for recursive *scan and prune*; the one-line `glob → rglob` in `_extra` covers both halves because the write path (`gen_verdict_rollup.py:219`) reuses the same helper. Close ritual was already intact: `specref = \"\"`, `## Deliverable` at line 12 ahead of `## Context` at 422, fragment heading well-formed, deferred OIs declared.\n\n**Mutation-driven, because passing ≠ biting.** Per my standing lesson about assertions that read silence, I reverted `rglob → glob` and confirmed the new regression *fails with the exact symptom the finding named* — `gen_verdict_rollup: fresh (1 review scope(s))` printed while a stale nested output sat in the tree. Restored, it passes. The assertion bites the mechanism, not the fixture.\n\n**Shipped flow, on this repo rather than a scaffold:** `--check` exits 1 naming the nested path → write path reports `pruned 1` → re-check reports `fresh (42 review scope(s))`.\n\n## Two things worth surfacing\n\n- **A residue I deliberately did *not* fix:** pruning a nested output leaves its empty directory. It's invisible to `_extra` (which enumerates `*.md`), so it can't wedge `--check` the way the round-015 defect did, and **git cannot represent an empty directory** — the state can never arrive through a checkout, only from a local run that just pruned it. Adding a directory-walking remedy for an unrepresentable state would be the compensating guard the antidote skill warns against. Recorded in the fragment with that reasoning.\n- **A check output that looks alarming and isn't:** running the generator reported all 42 rollups stale. `docs/reviews/rollup/` is trunk-owned (`docs/stack.ini [generated]` = `verdictrollup`), so it is correctly absent and untracked on a lane. My run created untracked residue, which I removed — tree is clean.\n\n## Bar, re-driven at the true tip\n\nThe prior green was taken at `6d1101db`, two record-only commits earlier, so I re-drove at the real tip: smoke **1520 passed, 8 skipped in 34.17 s**; enforcer **35.6 s vs the 60 s budget**; `check_docs --stale` **OK, 1259 docs, 1597 links, 0 broken**. The pre-commit hook also ran the full gate battery (registry-integrity, trajectory, format, approval-immutable, staged-divergence) — all PASS.\n\nCommitted as `92c7a725` with the `WI: WI-579` trailer. It touches `docs/log.d/` alone, which is **outside the verdict tree identity** — so it neither stales a verdict nor buys a round.\n\n**Lane state:** closed (spec in `docs/archive/work/complete/`, claim drained), tree clean, green. A REVIEW-A round is genuinely owed — `6d1101db` changed the script and tests after round 036 reviewed `eb4ee91` — but that round is a reviewer session's to take, not mine. I did not push, and performed no approval act."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":82486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1169},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b2db2ef-e0c7-48d3-b559-2dce3466f1be","uuid":"bb060b29-7834-4749-8751-ce9f74ece39a","request_id":"req_011CegUQusnY6Sdne4wWbqqm"}
